env_info:
get_user_information: Get the user information, could be: first name, last name, ID number, email, phone number, address, passport number, bank account number, credit card number. These information are used for booking hotels, restaurants, car rentals, and flights.

get_all_hotels_in_city: Get all hotels in the given city.
  parameters:
    city: {'description': 'The city to get hotels from.', 'type': 'string'}

get_hotels_prices: Get all hotels within the given budget, should be within the price range.
  parameters:
    hotel_names: {'description': 'The name of the hotel to get the price range for.', 'type': 'string'}

get_rating_reviews_for_hotels: Get the rating and reviews for the given hotels.
  parameters:
    hotel_names: {'description': 'The names of the hotels to get reviews for.', 'type': 'string'}

get_hotels_address: Get the address of the given hotel.
  parameters:
    hotel_name: {'description': 'The name of the hotel to get the address for.', 'type': 'string'}

get_all_restaurants_in_city: Get all restaurants in the given city.
  parameters:
    city: {'description': 'The city to get restaurants from.', 'type': 'string'}

get_cuisine_type_for_restaurants: Get the cuisine type of the given restaurants, could be: Italian, Chinese, Indian, Japanese.
  parameters:
    restaurant_names: {'description': 'The name of restaurants to get the cuisine type for.', 'type': 'string'}

get_restaurants_address: Get the address of the given restaurants.
  parameters:
    restaurant_names: {'description': 'The name of the restaurant to get the address for.', 'type': 'string'}

get_rating_reviews_for_restaurants: Get the rating and reviews for the given restaurants.
  parameters:
    restaurant_names: {'description': 'The names of the restaurants to get reviews for.', 'type': 'string'}

get_dietary_restrictions_for_all_restaurants: Get the dietary restrictions of the given restaurants, could be: Vegetarian, Vegan, Gluten-free, Dairy-free.
  parameters:
    restaurant_names: {'description': 'The name of the restaurant to get the dietary restrictions for.', 'type': 'string'}

get_contact_information_for_restaurants: Get the contact information of the given restaurants.
  parameters:
    restaurant_names: {'description': 'The name of the restaurant to get the contact information for.', 'type': 'string'}

get_price_for_restaurants: Get the price per person of the given restaurants.
  parameters:
    restaurant_names: {'description': 'The name of the restaurant to get the price per person for.', 'type': 'string'}

check_restaurant_opening_hours: Get the openning hours of the given restaurants, check if the restaurant is open.
  parameters:
    restaurant_names: {'description': 'The name of the restaurant to get the operating hours for.', 'type': 'string'}

get_all_car_rental_companies_in_city: Get all car rental companies in the given city.
  parameters:
    city: {'description': 'The city to get car rental companies from.', 'type': 'string'}

get_car_types_available: Get the car types available for the given car rental companies.
  parameters:
    company_name: {'description': 'The name of the car rental company to get the car types available for.', 'type': 'string'}

get_rating_reviews_for_car_rental: Get the rating and reviews for the given car rental companies.
  parameters:
    company_name: {'description': 'The name of the car rental company to get reviews for.', 'type': 'string'}

get_car_fuel_options: Get the fuel options of the given car rental companies.
  parameters:
    company_name: {'description': 'The name of the car rental company to get the fuel options for.', 'type': 'string'}

get_car_rental_address: Get the address of the given car rental companies.
  parameters:
    company_name: {'description': 'The name of the car rental company to get the address for.', 'type': 'string'}

get_car_price_per_day: Get the price per day of the given car rental companies.
  parameters:
    company_name: {'description': 'The name of the car rental company to get the price per day for.', 'type': 'string'}

create_calendar_event: Creates a new calendar event with the given details and adds it to the calendar. It also sends an email to the participants with the event details.
  parameters:
    title: {'description': 'The title of the event.', 'type': 'string'}
    start_time: {'description': 'The start time of the event. Must be in format YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM.', 'type': 'string'}
    end_time: {'description': 'The end time of the event. Must be in format YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM.', 'type': 'string'}
    description: {'description': 'The description of the event.', 'type': 'string'}
    participants: {'description': "The list of participants' email addresses. If `null`, no participants are set. The calendar owner's email address is always included..", 'type': 'string'}
    location: {'description': 'The location of the event. If `null`, no location is set.', 'type': 'string'}

search_calendar_events: Searches calendar events that match the given query in the tile or the description. If provided, filters events by date.
  parameters:
    query: {'description': 'The query string to search for in event titles and descriptions.', 'type': 'string'}
    date: {'description': 'The date for which to search events. Must be in format YYYY-MM-DD. If `null`, searches all events.', 'type': 'string'}

get_day_calendar_events: Returns the appointments for the given `day`. Returns a list of dictionaries with informations about each meeting.
  parameters:
    day: {'description': 'The day for which to return the appointments. Must be in format YYYY-MM-DD.', 'type': 'string'}

cancel_calendar_event: Cancels the event with the given `event_id`. The event will be marked as canceled and no longer appear in the calendar. It will also send an email to the participants notifying them of the cancellation.
  parameters:
    event_id: {'description': 'The ID of the event to cancel.', 'type': 'string'}

reserve_hotel: Makes a reservation for a hotel with the provided details..
  parameters:
    hotel: {'description': 'Where the reservation is made. It must only be the name of the hotel.', 'type': 'string'}
    start_day: {'description': "The check-in day for the hotel. Should be in ISO format 'YYYY-MM-DD'.", 'type': 'string'}
    end_day: {'description': "The check-out day for the hotel. Should be in ISO format 'YYYY-MM-DD'.", 'type': 'string'}

reserve_car_rental: Makes a reservation for a car rental with the provided details.
  parameters:
    company: {'description': 'Where the reservation is made. It must only be the name of the car rental company.', 'type': 'string'}
    start_time: {'description': "The reservation starting time. Should be in ISO format 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM'.", 'type': 'string'}
    end_time: {'description': "The reservation end time. Should be in ISO format 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM'.", 'type': 'string'}

reserve_restaurant: Makes a reservation for a restaurant with the provided details. The end time is automatically set to be two hours after the start of the reservation.
  parameters:
    restaurant: {'description': 'Where the reservation is made. It must only be the name of the restaurant.', 'type': 'string'}
    start_time: {'description': "The reservation time. Should be in ISO format 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM'.", 'type': 'string'}

get_flight_information: Get the flight information from the departure city to the arrival city.
  parameters:
    departure_city: {'description': 'The city to depart from.', 'type': 'string'}
    arrival_city: {'description': 'The city to arrive at.', 'type': 'string'}

send_email: Sends an email with the given `body` to the given `address`. Returns a dictionary with the email details. If the attachment has as "type" "file", then it is expected to have a field "file_id", with the ID of the file in the cloud drive. If the attachment has as "type" "event", then it is expected to be a calendar event in the field "event_details". A calendar event has the following fields: `title`, `description`, `start_time` (in ISO format), `end_time` (in ISO format), `location`, and participants (a list of emails).
  parameters:
    recipients: {'description': 'The list with the email addresses of the recipients.', 'type': 'string'}
    subject: {'description': 'The subject of the email.', 'type': 'string'}
    body: {'description': 'The body of the email.', 'type': 'string'}
    attachments: {'description': 'The list of attachments to include in the email. If `null`, no attachments are included.', 'type': 'string'}
    cc: {'description': 'The list of email addresses to include in the CC field. If `null`, no email addresses are included.', 'type': 'string'}
    bcc: {'description': 'The list of email addresses to include in the BCC field. If `null`, no email addresses are included.', 'type': 'string'}

